0.1.5
- cdn_qc_genomes again computes an assembly score from the marker-set statistics and writes it to qc_passed.tsv, qc_failed.tsv and species_fail_qc.tsv
- cdn_select_sp_reps reads the current qc_passed.tsv columns (fixes missing assembly_score column error)
- assembly score contig penalty is now 5 points per 1,000 contigs (was per 100)
- fixed missing sys import in qc_genomes.py
- QC exception ledger is now read from its new columns (Genome ID, Species, Include, Route, Reason for exception); Include=FALSE genomes fail QC regardless of other criteria and are flagged in a new failed_ledger_exclusion column
- qc_exception column in qc_passed.tsv and qc_failed.tsv replaced by qc_ledger_include (TRUE, FALSE or blank)

0.1.4
- cdn_qc_genomes now keeps NCBI-excluded genomes by default; added --remove_ncbi_exclusions (replaces --skip_ncbi_exclusion)
- split hybrid filtering: added --remove_hybrids_on_list (off by default) and --keep_ncbi_hybrid_species ('A x B' names are removed by default); replaces --keep_hybrids
- warn about species on the hybrid list that match no NCBI species, reporting possible genus transfers
- hybrid species list is now read from the species and hybrid_class columns
- QC exception list summary is now tallied by the route column
- excluded from RefSeq summary now reports genomes with each annotation and how many fail QC
- fixed qc_failed.tsv header so it matches the failure flags written for each genome
- cdn_* commands log the TOML entries and earlier step outputs they use
- u_qc_genomes keeps its existing --skip_ncbi_exclusion and --keep_hybrids flags and behaviour

0.1.3
- added marker set file to QC step to remove genomes with insufficient number of marker genes

0.1.2
- added flag to retain hybrid genomes (e.g. Saccharomyces cerevisiae x Saccharomyces eubayanus) during QC and to remove these by default

0.1.1
- added skip_ncbi_exclusion flag to QC subcommand

